# AgentDesk Coding Rules — Pre-Flight Checklist

> **READ THIS BEFORE WRITING ANY CODE.**
> Source of truth: `/CLAUDE.md` Section 0. This file is a compact summary for quick reference.

---

## Rule 0-1: No Emoji in UI Components

- **NEVER** use emoji or unicode symbols in JSX/TSX.
- All icons must be inline SVG.
- Allowed exceptions: DB data values (`agent.avatar_emoji`), user-visible plain text content.

```tsx
// WRONG
<span>✓</span>  <button>▶ Run</button>  <span>⚠ Error</span>

// CORRECT
<svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" strokeWidth="2" strokeLinecap="round" strokeLinejoin="round">
  <polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/>
</svg>
```

## Rule 0-2: SVG Icon Conventions

```tsx
<svg
  width="16"                   // explicit px size (14/16/18)
  height="16"
  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
  fill="none"
  stroke="currentColor"       // inherit from parent CSS color
  strokeWidth="2"
  strokeLinecap="round"
  strokeLinejoin="round"
>
```

- No `1rem`/`1em` sizes — always px.
- No hardcoded hex colors inside SVG — use `currentColor` + parent `style={{ color: "..." }}`.

## Rule 0-3: TypeScript Zero Tolerance

- Run `npx tsc -b --noEmit` after every change. **Zero errors required.**
- **Never use `any`** unless wrapping a third-party boundary with no types. Must add justifying comment.
- **Never use `as Foo`** to silence errors. Fix the root type instead.
- Remove unused imports immediately.

## Rule 0-4: No New Files Without Justification

- Prefer editing existing files.
- New files only when: > 80 lines OR reused in 2+ places OR clearly separate concern.
- Do NOT create `utils.ts`, `helpers.ts`, or `constants.ts` barrel files for one-off functions.

## Rule 0-5: DB Migrations — Append Only

- **NEVER** edit or delete an existing migration entry.
- Always append at the end of `migrations-e-recent.ts`.
- ID format: `YYYY-MM-DD-NNN-short-description`
- **Last applied ID**: `2026-03-28-013-project-app-type` → next: `2026-03-28-014-*`
- Wrap DDL in `try { ... } catch { /* already exists */ }`.

## Rule 0-6: Component State Rules

- No `useState` for data that belongs in a Zustand store.
- `useCallback`/`useMemo` only when genuinely expensive or referentially unstable.
- Modal/overlay state in `uiStore` if triggered from multiple places.

## Rule 0-7: API + Server Rules

- All new routes go in sub-routers under `server/modules/routes/`.
- Document every new endpoint in `docs/specs/api.md` (bump version).
- Responses: `res.json({ ok: true, ... })` success / `res.status(4xx).json({ error: "snake_case" })` error.
- **No `console.log`** in server code — use pino logger.

---

## File Length

- Single file should be **300 lines or less**.
- Over 300 lines → split by responsibility: hooks → `useXxx.ts`, sub-UI → `XxxSection.tsx`, types → `types.ts`.

## Naming

| Target | Convention | Example |
|--------|-----------|---------|
| Components/files | PascalCase | `ChatEditorModal.tsx` |
| Hooks | `use` + camelCase | `useCliUsage` |
| Functions/variables | camelCase | `handleCanvasSelect` |
| Constants | UPPER_SNAKE_CASE | `MIN_OFFICE_W` |
| Types/interfaces | PascalCase | `OfficeViewProps` |
| Boolean state | `is`/`has`/`show` prefix | `isOverviewMode` |

## Type Imports

- Type-only imports must use `import type { ... }`.
- **Never** use inline type references: `import("...").TypeName`.

---

## Verification (Run Before Completing Any Task)

```bash
npx tsc -b --noEmit    # zero errors required
pnpm lint               # minimize warnings
pnpm test               # all tests pass
```
